@page
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy";
}
<article class="prose">
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p class="lede">Huddle Board doesn't collect your information. There's no account,
    no sign-in, no analytics and no advertising. Everything you make in the app stays
    on your tablet.</p>
  <p>This policy covers the website at kidsflaghuddle.org, the app at
    kidsflaghuddle.org/app/, the standalone app file, and the Huddle Board app on
    Google Play, which opens the same app. Last updated 31 October 2026.</p>

  <h2>What stays on your tablet</h2>
  <p>Your deck, play names, notes, saved weeks, hidden plays, drawn plays, settings
    and game log are kept in your browser's own storage on the device. None of it
    is sent to us or anyone else. We can't see it, and we couldn't recover it for
    you if you lost it.</p>
  <p>Remove it any time from <b>Setup → Tablet</b>: <b>Start over</b> resets the
    setup, and the game log has its own Clear. Clearing the browser's site data or
    uninstalling the app removes all of it.</p>

  <h2>Sync files are yours to send</h2>
  <p><b>Sync tablets</b> exports your setup as a file. It goes only where you send
    it, using your tablet's share sheet or a download. The same goes for an exported
    game log. Huddle Board never uploads either one.</p>

  <h2>Kids' information</h2>
  <p>The app is shown to children, but it doesn't ask for, store or send anything
    about them. The only names in it are play names and positions such as WIDE BLUE.
    If you type a player's name into a play note, it stays on your tablet like
    everything else.</p>

  <h2>What our server sees</h2>
  <p>Like any website, the server that hosts Huddle Board (Microsoft Azure) receives
    the usual details of each request: your IP address, the page asked for, the time
    and your browser type. We use them only to keep the site running and fix
    problems. We don't use them to identify you, and we don't sell or share them.
    The hosting platform may set a technical cookie to route your requests; Huddle
    Board itself sets no cookies.</p>
  <p>Once the app is installed and working offline, using it sends nothing at all.
    It contacts the server only to download the app or check for an update.</p>

  <h2>Other services</h2>
  <p>The site and the app load their typefaces from Google Fonts, so your browser
    asks Google's servers for them when you're online. Google receives your IP
    address and browser details as part of that request; see
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google's privacy policy</a>.
    Offline, the app uses your tablet's built-in fonts instead.</p>
  <p>Links to <a href="https://github.com/crawfordjustin/huddle-board">GitHub</a>
    and <a href="https://ko-fi.com/justincrawford">Ko-fi</a> take you to those sites,
    which have their own privacy policies. If you report an issue or support the
    project there, we see what those sites show us, such as your username or the
    name you give with a donation.</p>

  <h2>Changes and questions</h2>
  <p>If this policy changes, the new version will be posted on this page with a new
    date. Its history is also on
    <a href="https://github.com/crawfordjustin/huddle-board">GitHub</a>.
    Questions are welcome: see <a href="/contact">Contact us</a>.</p>
</article>
